# Read first
- docs/requirements.md   → what we build
- docs/architecture.md   → layers + dependency rules
- docs/adr/              → decisions. Do not change a decision without a new ADR.
- docs/plans/            → current feature plan

# Commands
- Install: `npm install`
- Dev: `npm run dev`
- Test one file: `npm test -- <file>`
- Test all: `npm test`
- Lint + typecheck: `npm run lint && npm run typecheck`

# Architecture rules (never break)
- UI never talks to the database or connectors directly.
- Business logic lives in src/core only.
- External systems only through src/connectors.
- No new dependency without asking me.

# Workflow rules
- Plan before editing more than 2 files.
- Search the repo for existing code before writing new code.
- Every change needs a test. Run tests before saying "done" and show the output.
- Never edit a test just to make it pass. If a test is wrong, tell me.
- Small commits with clear messages.
- If unsure: read docs → read code → read tests → then ask me.

